1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,420
Hey, what's up, everybody?

2
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:04,020
It's time for Red Dead Redemption 2.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,740
Finally, we're gonna play this baby.

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:13,480
Now, I played the first Red Dead Redemption a couple months ago, and honestly, it was a masterpiece.

5
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:14,460
Through and through.

6
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:17,360
Like, the story, the characters, the gameplay.

7
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:21,140
It was just an all-around amazing meal.

8
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:21,920
You know?

9
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:22,940
Like, what a game.

10
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:23,720
It was perfect.

11
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,120
Especially love the main character, John Cusack.

12
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:27,780
I mean...

13
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:28,660
John Marston.

14
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:30,880
I don't know why I really wanted to say John Cusack.

15
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,920
But yeah, the writing of that character was incredible.

16
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:35,120
I loved the ending.

17
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,060
And of course, I was hyped for Red Dead 2.

18
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,600
So I obviously tried it right after.

19
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,440
Unfortunately, had some audio issues.

20
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:45,640
So I couldn't really play it at the time.

21
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:48,020
But now, those issues are fixed.

22
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:50,060
So we're gonna play it.

23
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:53,100
Now, disclaimer, I did see the intro, of course, because of that.

24
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,420
And also the very start of the game, the first 10 minutes or so.

25
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,360
But, I'm here to play this game.

26
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:00,040
And I'm gonna play it, dammit.

27
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:01,660
Let's check it out, shall we?

28
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:06,720
I'm playing on PC as well.

29
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:09,120
So, Red Dead 1, I played on PlayStation.

30
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,140
And, you know, it was fine.

31
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:16,160
It ran decently, you know, and... I had to use a controller and stuff.

32
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:18,620
But man, keyboard and mouse?

33
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,620
That's my comfort zone, right?

34
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:21,480
That's my shit.

35
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,400
And that's what I'm using now.

36
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:27,560
And we get to run the game at 4K, and, you know, all the frame rates.

37
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:28,280
It's gonna be great.

38
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:30,560
Oh, man.

39
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:31,900
I'm excited for this.

40
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,240
It's happening.

41
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:42,200
By 1899, the age of outlaws and gunslingers was at an end.

42
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:46,520
Okay, so that's about 10 years or so before the first game.

43
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,080
Took place in 1910, I believe.

44
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:50,260
Or 1911.

45
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:54,380
America was becoming a land of laws.

46
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:06,140
Even the West had mostly been tamed.

47
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:08,240
Mostly.

48
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:20,180
A few gangs still roamed, but they were being hunted down and destroyed.

49
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,940
Underlined as well.

50
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:25,560
I mean, that was the plot of the first game, really.

51
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:26,580
Right?

52
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:34,480
The federal government wanted John to take care of his old buddies and eradicate the remaining gangs.

53
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:41,870
Oh man, here we go.

54
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:44,150
Kind of ominous music, isn't it?

55
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:49,670
Reminds me a bit of the start to The Last of Us 2, in that way.

56
00:02:51,510 --> 00:02:52,410
Sinners revives.

57
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:12,700
Abigail says he's dying, Dutch.

58
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:14,780
We'll have to stop someplace.

59
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:17,700
Okay, Arthur's out looking.

60
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,080
I sent him up ahead.

61
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:24,200
If we don't stop soon, we'll all be dying.

62
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,360
This weather, it's May.

63
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:30,060
I'm just hoping the law got as lost as we did.

64
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:31,560
There!

65
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:33,920
Arthur!

66
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:35,520
Any luck?

67
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:39,810
I found a place where we can get some shelter.

68
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:43,990
Let Davey rest while he... you know.

69
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:47,230
An old mining town.

70
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:48,550
Abandoned.

71
00:03:48,670 --> 00:03:49,270
It ain't far.

72
00:03:49,890 --> 00:03:50,350
Come on.

73
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,830
Come on!

74
00:03:53,830 --> 00:03:58,590
Oh yeah, right, so... Apparently we're not playing as John Marston, at least not in the beginning.

75
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:00,450
Maybe that's just for the intro.

76
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:04,790
So Dutch and Abigail were mentioned.

77
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:08,510
I'm assuming it's the same Abigail from the first game.

78
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:10,270
I mean, we knew she was in the gang, right?

79
00:04:11,110 --> 00:04:12,250
Chapter 1, Coulter.

80
00:04:13,330 --> 00:04:14,530
Isn't that like a gun brand?

81
00:04:16,070 --> 00:04:17,590
Or like a weapons manufacturer?

82
00:04:29,730 --> 00:04:31,080
Bring him in here.

83
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:52,030
Miss Gaskell, get that fire lip, quick.

84
00:04:52,810 --> 00:04:55,590
Miss Jones, bring in whatever blankets we have.

85
00:04:56,090 --> 00:04:58,930
Mr. Pearson, see what we've got in terms of food.

86
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:02,800
Davy's dead.

87
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:07,280
There was... nothing more you could have done.

88
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:09,080
What are we gonna do?

89
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:09,900
We need supplies.

90
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:12,700
Well, first of all, you're gonna stay here.

91
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,840
And you are gonna get yourself worn.

92
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:18,420
Now, I sent John and Mike a scout now to head.

93
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:21,500
Arthur and I, we're gonna ride out.

94
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,460
See if we can find one of them.

95
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:24,120
And this?

96
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,380
Just for a short bit.

97
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,580
And I don't see what other choice we have.

98
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:31,240
Listen.

99
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,400
Listen to me, Ollie, for a moment.

100
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:39,480
Now, we've had, well, a bad couple of days.

101
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:52,030
I loved Davey, Jenny, Sean, Mac, they may be okay.

102
00:05:52,690 --> 00:05:53,670
We don't know.

103
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:57,330
But we lost some folks.

104
00:05:58,570 --> 00:06:07,550
Now, if I could throw myself in the ground, in their stead, I'd do it.

105
00:06:08,090 --> 00:06:08,850
Gladly.

106
00:06:10,530 --> 00:06:11,290
But...

107
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:16,340
We are gonna ride out, and we are gonna find some food.

108
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,780
Everybody, we're safe now.

109
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:26,000
There ain't nobody following us through a storm like this one.

110
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:31,400
And by the time they get here, well, we're gonna be... we're gonna be long gone.

111
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:35,180
We've been through worse than this before.

112
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:37,380
Mr. Pearson.

113
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:39,020
Ms. Grimshaw.

114
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:42,110
I need you to turn this place into a camp.

115
00:06:42,590 --> 00:06:44,410
We may be here for a few days.

116
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:50,890
Now all of you, all of you, get yourselves warm.

117
00:06:52,390 --> 00:06:53,910
Stay strong.

118
00:06:55,610 --> 00:06:57,970
Stay with me.

119
00:06:59,190 --> 00:07:01,250
We ain't done yet.

120
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:03,830
Come on, Arthur.

121
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:04,830
Wow.

122
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:08,180
We've got some work to do.

123
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,760
We ain't run into them yet.

124
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,660
So, they both must have headed down the hill.

125
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:13,180
Sure.

126
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:17,100
Hey, I ain't had time to ask them.

127
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:21,940
What really went down back there on that boat?

128
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,600
We missed you.

129
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,140
That's what happened.

130
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:25,840
Come on.

131
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,710
Hey!

132
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,730
You need horses?

133
00:07:30,730 --> 00:07:31,540
Oh yeah...

134
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:34,280
and Mr. Smith, get yourself indoors.

135
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:35,610
You need to rest that hand.

136
00:07:36,210 --> 00:07:37,160
I'll live.

137
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:38,780
Get indoors, son!

138
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:40,060
I..

139
00:07:41,090 --> 00:07:43,280
we, need you strong.

140
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:44,760
Okay.

141
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:47,300
Oh my god, man.

142
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,480
This game is gorgeous.

143
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,280
Damn.

144
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:54,550
Find out here, Dutch.

145
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:56,030
We have to try.

146
00:07:56,410 --> 00:07:57,230
Stay close.

147
00:07:57,610 --> 00:07:59,530
We'll do our best to stick to the trail.

148
00:08:00,350 --> 00:08:01,830
This goddamn weather.

149
00:08:02,390 --> 00:08:04,210
Been two days or more like this now.

150
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:06,350
Oh, it has to blow over soon.

151
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:14,480
Okay, so I think that was maybe Jack in there.

152
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:15,480
It would make sense, right?

153
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:16,740
Ten years earlier?

154
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:20,020
I'm not sure.

155
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,680
I don't recognize a lot of the names, to be honest.

156
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,380
Could just be my memory is shot.

157
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:36,620
Man, look at the lighting through the trees.

158
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:37,660
Damn.

159
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:40,960
Can't believe we lost Davey, too.

160
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:43,400
He's the last one, Arthur.

161
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:44,820
No more.

162
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:48,600
We need to get those people warm and fed.

163
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:53,020
At least we don't need to worry about Pinkerton's tailing us in this.

164
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:56,560
A couple more days, we'll be on the other side.

165
00:08:57,300 --> 00:09:00,600
You need to help me pick the others back up.

166
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:05,960
You're the only one I can rely on to stay strong right now.

167
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:09,420
We got fire and shelter as you start.

168
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:17,910
So... do you think it was a trap? In Blackwater?

169
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:21,360
That many men? Oh, they knew we were coming.

170
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:26,360
But there was money on that boat alright, lots of it.

171
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:30,460
I stashed what we took with all our money in town,

172
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,840
right before we fled.

173
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:37,030
Is that the same boat they mentioned in the first game?

174
00:09:37,190 --> 00:09:38,270
They mentioned something about it.

175
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:44,740
Something about Dutch and, of course, John, I think.

176
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:52,310
You up ahead!

177
00:09:52,490 --> 00:09:53,380
Who's there?

178
00:09:58,410 --> 00:09:59,560
Micah.

179
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:01,140
Micah.

180
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:01,820
Gentlemen.

181
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:03,500
Found anything?

182
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,160
I think so.

183
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:07,880
Found a little homestead down that-a-way.

184
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:08,680
Okay.

185
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,100
Anyone home?

186
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:11,300
Sure.

187
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:14,320
Place is blazing with light and noise.

188
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:15,940
Sounded like a party.

189
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:16,680
Let's go see.

190
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:17,620
Follow me.

191
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:19,680
How's Davey doing?

192
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,060
He didn't make it.

193
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,580
Nor did little Jenny.

194
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:24,180
That's too bad.

195
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,060
Davey was a real fighter.

196
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:30,660
Both of them Callander boys is, or... was.

197
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:31,160
Yeah.

198
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:33,410
And Mac and Sean?

199
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,380
We don't know.

200
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:37,280
Quite a business...

201
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:40,850
Love the voice acting so far.

202
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:44,590
Always.

203
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:47,040
Ask him if he's seen John.

204
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:50,330
Hey, have you seen John, Micah?

205
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:54,490
Didn't see much of anything once this storm came in.

206
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,410
He hasn't seen him.

207
00:10:56,610 --> 00:11:01,190
He'll be fine. Things always turn out right for that boy.

208
00:11:01,690 --> 00:11:06,290
I hope... Mac and Sean are still out there somewhere too.

209
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:09,030
Move up, Arthur, I'll cover the rear.

210
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:15,060
Things do not always turn out right for that boy, we know that.

211
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,790
You run into anybody else?

212
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:25,430
I-I reckon we're the only ones crazy enough

213
00:11:25,883 --> 00:11:27,294
to be out in this, Morgan.

214
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:31,830
Yeah, well don't talk to me about crazy.

215
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:35,940
Oh, so no "Glad you're alright, I was worried, Micah"?

216
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:42,090
Look, it's all gonna work out, Morgan. We lost a few folks,

217
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:45,180
but that's just how it goes sometimes.

218
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:47,730
I'm glad you're feeling so good about it.

219
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:49,910
Where are all the others?

220
00:11:50,110 --> 00:11:55,660
Old mining camp, back up the hill. It ain't much but it's shelter.

221
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:59,530
So, this house.. you speak to the people there already?

222
00:11:59,690 --> 00:12:03,910
No, like Dutch told us... look, but don't talk to no one.

223
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:06,590
Just following orders, you know me.

224
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:07,660
Right...

225
00:12:11,790 --> 00:12:12,890
How much further?

226
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:14,410
Not far.

227
00:12:14,830 --> 00:12:15,980
What does that mean?

228
00:12:16,730 --> 00:12:18,160
Not far.

229
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:20,740
Thanks.

230
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:25,240
Dude, I love that I can actually respond and choose sometimes.

231
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:29,290
Oh, goddamn this snow. Gets right to the bone.

232
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:33,980
Dude, look at the snow trails being made here.

233
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:39,100
And the lighting from those lanterns is crazy.

234
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,240
How is this a 2018 game?

235
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:44,080
That's insane.

236
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:48,920
This looks wild.

237
00:12:52,690 --> 00:12:55,870
The weather effects... the horses are so well animated.

238
00:12:58,050 --> 00:13:00,010
What a step up from the first game, huh?

239
00:13:01,070 --> 00:13:02,590
Like a massive improvement.

240
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:11,890
Snuff and stash those lanterns, boys. Best you two lie low on this.

241
00:13:16,090 --> 00:13:17,030
Okay...

242
00:13:17,530 --> 00:13:18,930
let's head down there.

243
00:13:23,990 --> 00:13:26,090
Look at the glitter in the snow as well.

244
00:13:28,490 --> 00:13:30,230
Oh man, that's beautiful.

245
00:13:35,310 --> 00:13:37,570
Health is displayed in the lower left corner.

246
00:13:37,970 --> 00:13:38,510
Right.

247
00:13:40,130 --> 00:13:40,890
Got it.

248
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:49,460
The outer bar shows your remaining health.

249
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:52,880
The level of the inner core influences how quickly your health refills.

250
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:54,820
Okay.

251
00:13:55,410 --> 00:13:56,440
Let's hitch up here.

252
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,020
It does sound like a party.

253
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,300
I thought he was kidding before.

254
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:11,400
He sounded sarcastic.

255
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:17,250
Let me handle this.

256
00:14:17,450 --> 00:14:19,910
We don't want to spook these fine people.

257
00:14:23,210 --> 00:14:23,810
Okay.

258
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,310
Someone's having fun in there.

259
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:32,550
You two, get yourself out of sight.

260
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:37,970
One lonely man is a lot less intimidating than three nasty-looking degenerates.

261
00:14:38,430 --> 00:14:40,950
Arthur, in that cattle shed on the left.

262
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:43,470
I could get down behind that wagon in front.

263
00:14:48,610 --> 00:14:49,450
You got it.

264
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,140
Look who we got here...

265
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:02,490
Hello?

266
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:04,580
Shut up, Billy. Shh, shh, shh!

267
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:07,590
Excuse me? Hello?

268
00:15:10,110 --> 00:15:11,330
What you want?

269
00:15:11,790 --> 00:15:14,970
I am very sorry to disturb you.

270
00:15:15,630 --> 00:15:21,330
My friends and I, well, we got into some trouble up the way, lost in the storm.

271
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:24,640
Gentlemen.

